WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.060
<b>Nellis Army Base, USA</b>

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:20.370
Man, it'd be faster to fly it there 
rather than using an air transport.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.600
How many mid-air refuels do 
you think that would take?

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.620
How far away do you think it is?

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.130
Yukon's in Alaska. The far North.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:30.840
Like I care.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.130
I don't give a damn about some 
UN base in the middle of nowhere.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:40.320
Come to think of it, I heard an American 
Eishi did something big in the USSR.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.380
Set the world-record for 
kills in his first fight.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:46.770
Still not interested?

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:48.770
Not at all.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.960
I'll just clean them all up at once.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:58.030
<b>Cross To Bear</b>

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:53.190
Accurate shots, and can tell 
where I'm going to move next.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.610
They're making this fun.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.740
We'll get close and wipe them out.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.240
Bao-Feng Flight, follow me!

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:06.780
Roger!

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.120
I'll take out their leader.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.920
You can have the rest.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:18.920
Roger!

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.680
Don't run away!

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:35.400
Look at that!

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.670
Wow!

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:41.200
A rocket boost right into an enemy 
that's a mobile artillery platform.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:42.970
They're just idiots.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.400
You think so?

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:48.410
Those unorthodox movements seem to 
have thrown the other pilot off.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.000
They've got guts and talent.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:55.340
I didn't know there were still 
people like that in this base.

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:58.460
That's a pretty fast TSF.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:03.130
Yeah, it's based off the Viper, no, the F-16.

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:04.540
As for its hand-to-hand...

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:08.750
Duh! It's tiny so of course it's fast.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:13.980
That's right. The tiny ones 
always flit around a lot.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.980
Are you picking a fight with me?

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.240
I'm talking about TSFs.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:20.560
Or what?

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.040
You'd rather be called Jumpy than Chobi?

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.080
What?

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:25.910
Stop it you two.

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.530
Ibrahim's glaring at you.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:35.040
I'm still amazed the brass agreed 
to participate in this farce.

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:39.640
Members of each development team are working 
hard every day to improve their TSFs,

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:44.300
to defeat the BETA and 
take back their homelands.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:49.070
But a closed environment can 
sometimes hinder growth.

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:54.180
Thus, the UN Military has prepared an 
opportunity for you to test each other's mettle:

00:04:54.670 --> 00:05:00.250
The TSF General Evaluation 
Program, The Blue Flag Exercise.

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:04.440
A mock combat tournament between TSFs?

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.860
The companies making them just 
want to compete with each other.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.080
I understand, Commander.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.240
My job is to get the Shiranui finished, that's all.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:21.790
But what good is data from fighting other 
humans going to do on the front lines?

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.590
I can't believe we're halting 
development to focus on this.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.100
And it's thanks to them that we can 
go and play in training exercises!

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.990
This is how she felt back there, wasn't it?

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:36.020
Oh?

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:39.070
I understand how you feel, but 
we're in the middle of a mission.

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:40.740
Save it for later.

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:44.960
They say the eyes are a window to the soul.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:46.920
You were staring at Princess Yui weren't you?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:52.950
I thought things were a little odd between 
you two since we got back from Russia.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:55.130
You finally nailed her?

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.920
I know that feeling.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:59.290
The fact that she didn't like you at 
first just makes it hotter doesn't it?

00:05:59.560 --> 00:06:02.060
Shut up, damn it!

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:03.550
Me and Yui aren't like that!

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:11.340
Hey, everybody, he just 
called Lt. Takamura "Yui."

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.810
And he was gazing at her 
and saying "Je t'aime."

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.770
I did not say Je t'aime.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:20.480
- You sure?

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.610
- Is that the problem here?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:23.610
Stop goofing off during a briefing!

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:24.690
Don't read too much into it.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:32.950
The results of this test may cause the XFJ 
Project to be scaled back or worse, canceled.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.480
I hate to say it,

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:39.500
but what happened with the Type 99 has given 
a lot of strength to the project's opponents.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.580
But the remains...

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:43.210
Yes, they were sent back to us.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.350
And two days later, which is unusually fast.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:49.720
Given the time they had it's impossible 
for them to have analyzed it.

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:51.960
But that's all the more reason.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.140
Yes, it's very strange.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.760
What did the USSR want so badly it 
was willing to sacrifice so much?

00:06:59.880 --> 00:07:02.000
Am I simply being paranoid?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.220
Was there no plot?

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.650
But because of that my uncle's plan...

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.750
This is all because I insisted 
on taking the cannon.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:12.080
I'm sorry.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.680
I'm the one who approved 
it. Don't worry about it.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.410
But...

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:21.050
There's always been a strong nationalist 
faction who wanted to build it entirely domestically.

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:26.090
Since we decided to go ahead with this anyway, 
our only option is to go forward no matter what.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:27.100
Yes.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:29.610
Just like he did.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:33.070
I won't give up either.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:40.060
Then we'll give the nationalists what they 
want and show results in the Blue Flag Exercises.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:44.920
We'll show them that the XFJ Project 
is the right choice for the Empire.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.820
Sir?

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:51.050
That's a surprise.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:55.980
Once you realized you made a mistake 
you always used to dwell on it forever.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:58.140
This isn't the time...

00:07:58.140 --> 00:07:59.330
What happened?

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.190
Did you find a boy you like over there?

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.740
N-No!

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:07.980
I've been given a huge responsibility, I 
couldn't waste time on such frivolities...

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.380
I see you've still got your 
father's hard-headedness.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.020
Uncle!

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:19.760
Honestly, what is wrong with him?

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:24.770
I couldn't fall in love at an 
important time like this...

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:36.220
Yuuya...

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:39.230
Oh no.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:40.870
Lt. Takamura?

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:44.750
Ensign Bremer.

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:47.120
Um, are you okay?

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:48.080
Do you not feel well?

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:50.890
No, I am extremely fine.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.790
Do you need something?

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:59.450
Yes, I had a suggestion for tonight's party 
celebrating our return from Kamchatsky.

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:00.780
Suggestion?

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.520
Looks like a great party.

00:09:08.350 --> 00:09:11.020
Ugh. There's too many people here.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.480
You really do hate these things.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:16.040
Have some fun!

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.540
Oh, Ensign Bridges.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.430
Welcome back!

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:23.040
I heard about your success!

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:25.120
Oh, it wasn't-

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.360
Why are you dressed like that, Tarisa?

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.380
You start working here?

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:33.760
Shut up.

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:37.710
Isn't she cute?

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.710
You can be a bunnygirl next, Tarisa!

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:42.510
Shut up! Dummy! Dummy! Dummy!

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:44.910
Wait!

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.770
Look at that asshole VG.

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:52.040
I won't let him have all the fun.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:52.830
Bye.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:56.570
Hey, Yuuya.

00:09:57.640 --> 00:09:58.890
Stella.

00:09:58.890 --> 00:09:59.910
Having fun?

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:01.320
I guess.

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:06.000
Are you...

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.910
D-Don't look at me.

00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:09.670
What?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.170
Don't stare at me, please.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:15.160
Sorry.

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.300
Let's sit down.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.310
We were cooking together 
in the kitchen back there.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:24.920
What's gotten into you?

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.330
Why go through all the trouble of cooking?

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:29.790
Cooking is a great change of pace.

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:30.810
Right, Lieutenant?

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:35.820
Creating something is very fulfilling.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:39.760
Especially if it makes someone happy.

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:41.980
Take a look.

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:44.990
Is this...

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:46.380
Yes.

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:51.440
This is called "niku-jaga", it's 
traditional Japanese home cooking.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.250
It's hot, so be careful.

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:55.250
Y-Yeah.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:01.500
Damn it. Mom told me she invented it.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:05.140
This is good.

00:11:05.610 --> 00:11:07.270
Mom, what is this?

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.770
It's something I invented.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:13.770
Seconds!

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:22.530
Did she think I wouldn't eat it otherwise?

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:25.370
Yuuya?

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:27.980
It's good.

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:30.080
It's very good, I'll admit it.

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:34.080
I see. My mother taught me how to make this.

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:37.160
I see. Your mother.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:41.150
You're actually supposed to cook it for a 
little longer so that the secret ingredient, pepper,

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.400
can spread throughout the whole thing.

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:44.470
Can I have another bowl?

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:47.950
There's still a lot left.

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:51.730
I can't bear to watch either of you.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:54.150
Look at you two!

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:58.400
Yuuya, there's other things 
you could say, right?

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:06.160
You look like you're having fun.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:10.650
I'm Lt. Cui Yifei, from 
the United Chinese Front.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:14.080
Show yourself, Yuuya Bridges.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:19.420
I'm Lt. Cui Yifei, from 
the United Chinese Front.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.920
Show yourself, Yuuya Bridges.

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:25.150
I'm Yuuya-

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:33.680
You're the hero with the world record?

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:34.860
No.

00:12:35.280 --> 00:12:38.200
That was the Type 99, it wasn't me...

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:40.200
Don't insult me.

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:45.200
You were able to wipe out the enemy on a 
crowded battlefield without hitting a single friendly.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.760
That was your talent.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:53.960
I thought it would make you pretty cocky, 
but I'm actually kind of impressed.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:57.980
You're an elite Eishi with the US military,

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.210
why are you on a Japanese Development Team?

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.380
What race are you anyway?

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:05.440
You look Asian.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:07.710
What race are you?

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:09.230
I'm...

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.720
Give up on this blockhead, Lieutenant.

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:15.310
If you just want a guy to sleep 
with there's a good one over there.

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:18.830
Shut up, Chihuahua.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:21.480
I'm not interested in 
Eishi with average scores.

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.760
What?

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.570
You've got an average score too!

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.080
What did you say?

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:31.740
Lt. Cui.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:35.980
I apologize for my men's rudeness.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:37.370
And who are you?

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:41.320
Lt. Takamura Yui, the 
leader of the XFJ project.

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:43.850
We're here to celebrate 
our safe return tonight.

00:13:43.850 --> 00:13:45.690
I'll ask you to resolve 
this matter peacefully...

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:49.890
Of course. I wasn't planning on pulling rank.

00:13:50.570 --> 00:13:51.820
Yuuya Bridges.

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.390
You haven't answered my question yet.

00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.390
I...

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:00.400
I'm a Japanese-American.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:05.360
I think we're going to get along.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:07.860
Alright.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.270
I'll play with you for 
real in the next match.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.220
<i>Zai jian.</i>

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:18.500
She was a tornado.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:21.240
Bao-Feng is a good name.

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:22.970
Then she's...

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:24.720
I see.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.510
I get to fight her?

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:29.370
This Blue Flag thing isn't all bad then.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:44.320
Did you have a nightmare, Inia?

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:48.820
Yuuya just went far away...

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:50.270
Bridges did?

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:52.480
I'm lonely.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:57.330
Don't worry, Inia. 
Bridges isn't going anywhere.

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:58.940
Really?

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:02.830
If that's what you want, I'll make it happen.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:06.480
You'll be with me forever?

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.340
Yes.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:09.340
Forever.

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.840
Goodnight, Inia.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:31.110
Christ.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.410
So your new hobby is 
staring at the 94 Second?

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.920
It's like you're in love.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:41.480
I'm sure that makes a certain person feel 
better than other things you could be doing.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:42.620
What are you talking about?

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:48.130
Well, thanks to your love and passion, 
the tuning for #2 is coming along nicely.

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:49.360
Yeah.

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:53.550
We can't start the team 
tests until it's ready.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:57.480
You really are in love with the 94 Second.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.140
It's not like that.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:04.750
Just, I feel like when I'm with it, I 
can climb as high as I'd ever want to.

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:08.150
You really have changed.

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.970
I don't know about that.

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:17.760
I hope so.

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:20.290
It was good that you came to the Yukon.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:34.620
Yeah.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:35.800
That's right.

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:37.720
It sure is.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:42.430
The Goddess of Alaska is 
letting you have all the fun.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.770
What are you talking about? Stop it!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:54.090
Was that asshole trying to kill me?

00:16:54.890 --> 00:16:56.120
Yuuya Bridges.

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.040
Cryska?

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:02.840
You looking for Inia?

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.040
How could you tell?

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.870
Can you read my mind?

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.440
Your mind?

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:11.130
Answer me, Bridges.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.310
How could you tell what I'm here for?

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:16.400
You're treating me like an idiot, aren't you?

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:18.110
I am not.

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:19.870
You were an idiot to begin with.

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:21.810
There's no point in calling 
attention to it now.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.000
Think about it.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:28.090
You never talk to me unless it's about Inia.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:29.580
That's it.

00:17:30.840 --> 00:17:33.320
Oh, that wasn't much fun at all.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.360
Don't try to make it fun.

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:41.830
You didn't answer right 
away, so it made me wonder.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.280
Cryska smiled?

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:46.460
So?

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.600
Is Inia here?

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.330
No, she's not.

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:51.530
I see.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.960
You were my best guess.

00:17:54.410 --> 00:17:55.200
I was?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:56.780
What do you mean?

00:17:57.130 --> 00:18:00.830
Inia likes you.

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:03.070
Bye.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:07.480
Oh, fine.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:14.980
What are you doing?

00:18:15.340 --> 00:18:16.780
What about you?

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:19.740
You've just been walking around this area.

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:25.240
She likes going around the Eurasian hangars.

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:27.120
So that's it.

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:29.660
But you've looked everywhere here.

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:31.040
Any other guesses?

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:36.650
In the worst case, she's gone to 
a bar or cafeteria in Lilfort.

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.380
Why is that the worst case?

00:18:39.660 --> 00:18:44.000
The Soviety Military doesn't let 
you go there without permission.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:45.140
I see.

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:47.560
So she's outright breaking the rules.

00:18:47.560 --> 00:18:48.970
I'm impressed, Inia.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:54.430
Well, if the two of them are really 
part of the privileged class,

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:56.830
nothing bad will happen even if she's caught.

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:02.590
But the military is everything to Cryska.

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:05.640
Anything that betrays that is tough.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:07.370
Me too.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.140
Being recognized in the 
military was all I had once.

00:19:11.840 --> 00:19:13.330
Until I came here.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:15.640
I'll go check Lilfort.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:18.270
You search the other hangars.

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:19.500
We'll meet back here in 2 hours.

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:21.690
Bridges, what are you talking about?

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:24.040
It'd be more efficient to split up.

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.850
Why would you...?

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.550
What are you planning?

00:19:27.550 --> 00:19:28.750
Nothing.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:30.640
This is normal.

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:33.150
Normal?

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:34.120
Yes.

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:35.900
Here, anyway.

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:47.870
We saw lots of pretty 
colors today, didn't we?

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:51.000
But I didn't see Yuuya.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.760
Yuuya and Yui's colors are the prettiest.

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:56.220
That's no fun.

00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.120
I didn't find her.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.280
I wonder if Cryska did.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:08.040
She's amazing, though.

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:10.720
She's always searching by herself, isn't she?

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:23.820
Is that a Russian song?

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:28.830
It's a little sad... but gentle.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:37.830
Bridges?

00:20:38.350 --> 00:20:39.340
Did you find Inia?

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:42.190
I guess you didn't, either.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:44.200
I'm starting to get worried.

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:45.840
I hope it's nothing.

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:47.640
Don't worry about it.

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:50.850
If something happens to her I'll know.

00:20:51.230 --> 00:20:52.460
What?

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:56.620
If you've got a handy little system 
like that at least put a GPS on her.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:59.110
Is it possible she went back 
to the Soviet Facilities?

00:20:59.800 --> 00:21:02.010
This has never happened before.

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:04.110
If she doesn't make it back before curfew...

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:08.140
The one thing she enjoys 
will be taken from her.

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:11.070
Okay. Let's take another look.

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:12.250
Bridges.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.860
Why are you doing all this for us?

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:16.410
Because I want to.

00:21:16.410 --> 00:21:19.630
That's impossible. What 
good does that do you?

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:23.130
I want to give back what was given to me...

00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:28.010
what I took.

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:31.870
That's all.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.020
Is that you, Yuuya?

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:42.160
I knew it! It's been ages!

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:45.020
Sharon? What are you doing here?

00:21:45.690 --> 00:21:46.410
You!

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:48.940
What's wrong?

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:52.870
You having too much fun to 
remember your old buddy?

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:54.280
Don't worry.

00:21:54.670 --> 00:21:57.040
I'll never forget that ugly face of yours.

00:21:58.250 --> 00:21:59.960
Happy to hear it.

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:01.670
Bridges, who is he?

00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:04.000
Leon Kuze.

00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:06.670
A Japanese-American like me.

00:22:08.650 --> 00:22:12.080
He was on my squad before I came here.

00:22:12.670 --> 00:22:14.720
Yeah, it was a long time ago.

00:22:17.820 --> 00:22:19.640
That's... the Raptor?

00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:26.110
The US Army 65th Combat 
Training Group Infinities!

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:31.450
Playtime is over, Yuuya.

00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:34.910
I'll clean you up. Nice and good.

00:24:07.550 --> 00:24:09.630
Bao Feng 1 to all units.

00:24:10.280 --> 00:24:11.900
You know the drill.

00:24:12.540 --> 00:24:17.470
Yuuya Bridges, let's see what you can do.

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:24.270
<b>Pale Blue Flame</b>

00:24:19.420 --> 00:24:21.440
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.030 --> 00:24:23.420
Pale Blue Flame
